# 30. SCORE DEFINITIONS

## 0–2

Not remotely launch-ready.

## 3–4

Large portions incomplete or broken.

## 5–6

Core system works, but major production risks remain.

## 7

Mostly functional, but meaningful weaknesses remain.

## 8

Strong implementation with remaining production gaps.

## 9

Very strong production candidate with only minor remaining issues.

## 10

Fully verified release candidate with no known material blockers and strong evidence across engineering, security, product, UX, UI, performance, and operations.

